# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# tracked text files to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for Python, but fatal
# for a script that runs inside a Linux container: the shebang is read as
# `/usr/bin/env sh\r`, and Docker fails with the fairly opaque
#   env: 'sh\r': No such file or directory
# The Dockerfile also strips CR defensively, so a clone with different settings
# still builds a working image.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
